> < disclaimer>
> a. I play nethack 3.4.0 with Qt interface.

> I have 5 food rations in my inventory under letter 'f'. There is 456
> rocks in a chest on the ground under letter 'r'.
> If I want to drop 3 food rations, I type 'd3f' and it works. Problem
> is, when I want to pick up 3 out of 456 rocks the game gives a menu,
> and '#loot 3r' just doesn't work: the game wants me to pick up all 456
> rocks.
> 
> Is there a workaround ? (other than 'be overtaxed, drop 3 rocks,
> reinsert 453 rocks in the chest, pick up 3 rocks', please)

If they're in a chest, you should be getting the Qt selection window when
you loot it. The hyphen at the far left is a quantity indicator; click on
that to bring up a dialog that will ask you precisely how many you want.

(This also works for dropping items.)

For completeness: If the rocks are on the ground, with nothing else, use
the keyboard and type [n3,] in order to pick up three; or force the game 
to use the qt selector box by dropping some other item.



